<div class="container">

  <header style="background: transparent; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; box-shadow: none; padding: 0 0 24px 0; color: inherit; display: block;">
    <h1>A General Education in Mathematics<span class="subtitle">The Middle Way</span></h1>
  </header>

  <p>
    <strong>Middle Way Mathematics (MWM)</strong> is a curriculum and foundational framework for a general education in mathematics. The curriculum targets all motivated students, providing a clear overview of the nature of modern mathematical thought. It is not designed to prepare students for technical STEM tracks; rather, its goal is to provide a conceptual and formal literacy that enables lifelong, thoughtful engagement with modern physical theories and popular science.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Epistemological Stance: Mathematics as a Formal Science</h2>

  <p>
    Mathematics is treated as a formal science whose home is a world of supposition. It serves as a bridge linking human intuition with empirical experience—an arena where we ask <em>"What if?"</em>, trace deductive consequences, and evaluate how effectively the resulting structures model physical observations.
  </p>

